# guile-skills --- template for .env.  Copy to .env; .env is never tracked.
#
#   cp .env.example .env && direnv allow .
#
# NO SECRETS IN EITHER FILE. Secrets come from pass; see docs/secrets.org and
# scripts/sync-secrets.sh.
#
# Values use ${VAR} only. direnv's dotenv parser expands ${HOME} and $HOME but
# NOT ${VAR:-default} -- it silently mangles that into ${HOME/.cache}, verified
# on direnv 2.35.0. Anything needing a fallback belongs in .envrc, which is real
# shell. Deriving from ${HOME} rather than writing /home/dsp-dr keeps this file
# correct on nexus, hydra, mac and pi, and under either login (dsp-dr/jwalsh).
#
# Every value here is optional: .envrc supplies the same defaults when .env is
# absent, which is what makes a fresh checkout on a new host work unchanged.

# Claude Code scratch space (intermediate results, agent task transcripts).
# The default lives under /tmp, which is swept on reboot and is small on nexus;
# a long session's scratch is worth keeping. .envrc creates this 0700 -- a REPL
# transcript contains whatever was evaluated.
CLAUDE_CODE_TMPDIR="${HOME}/.cache/claude-code/guile-skills"
